{
  "//": [
    "Which Synty clips are allowed to become AMG World emotes.",
    "",
    "This is a SAFETY file, not a taste file. AMG World is a shared space for",
    "real 9-13 year olds in classrooms, so an emote is not just an animation —",
    "it is something one child performs AT another. The Synty packs were built",
    "for general games and contain gestures that are fine in a shooter and not",
    "fine here.",
    "",
    "Excluded on purpose, with reasons, so nobody re-adds them by accident:",
    "  Aggressive_ThroatSlit, Angry_StranglingMotion - violent gestures",
    "  Aggressive_MenacingFists, Aggressive_Roar_*   - intimidation aimed at a person",
    "  Aggressive_ThumbsDown_Roman                    - the 'kill him' gesture",
    "  Celebrate_FingerGuns_*                         - gun gesture; schools treat this seriously",
    "  ALL Taunt_*  (LaughAndPoint, MockCrying,       - the entire category exists to mock",
    "                Raspberry, SlowClap,               another player. This is a bullying",
    "                HandShakeReject)                   vector in a classroom social space.",
    "  ALL Reproach_* (incl. HeadTap_YouCrazy)        - scolding / 'go away' / 'you're crazy'",
    "  Sway_Drunk_*, Drink_*                          - alcohol connotations",
    "  Pray_*                                         - religious; public-school neutrality",
    "  PickNose_*                                     - crude, and a point-and-laugh magnet",
    "  UsePhone_*                                     - 25 clips that need a phone prop",
    "  Eat_*                                          - needs a food prop to read",
    "  Affection_BlowKiss, Affection_CallMe           - flirtation between minors",
    "  Inspect_Hips                                   - body-focused",
    "  Posture_Aggressive_*                           - as above",
    "  *_RM / *_RMH / *_RMV                           - root-motion variants; position is",
    "                                                   driven in code, so these double up",
    "",
    "Adding to this list is fine. Removing an exclusion is a safeguarding",
    "decision — talk to Devon first.",
    "",
    "`hold` clips are stances the avatar keeps until it moves; everything else",
    "is a one-shot that returns to locomotion."
  ],

